d**: the real testnet ledger where wallet-backend halted. Two are **generated** by a standalone stellar-core v30.0.0, on the mainnet and testnet passphrases. The generated ones push the edges: a 64-byte payload (the longest allowed, a 165-character strkey), and a 29-byte payload that needs XDR padding."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options-7","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options#what-it-reproduces","content":"`make replay` feeds testnet ledgers 4437356–4437359 to three real wallet-backend builds through a mock stellar-rpc:"},"1625":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options-8","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options#what-it-reproduces","content":"| wallet-backend build                        | Expected verdict                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `79ea2acd`, \"upgrade to protocol 28\" (#715) | **stores the signer as 33 bytes**, losing the payload (#716) |","table":"table-0"},"1626":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options-9","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options#what-it-reproduces","content":"| wallet-backend build                                              | Expected verdict            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `6e5a5910`, \"reduce muxed addresses to their base account\" (#693) | **halts** at ledger 4437357 |","table":"table-0"},"1627":{"id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-set-options-10","page_id":"/docs/corpus/entries/signer-signed-payload-