7":94,"2188":92,"2189":91,"2190":1405,"2191":14,"2192":1097,"2193":1235,"2194":1142,"2195":1193,"2196":1456,"2197":2325,"2198":829,"2199":1124,"2200":1465,"2201":1160,"2202":16,"2203":83,"2204":86,"2205":85,"2206":84,"2207":87,"2208":1757,"2209":1453,"2210":1478,"2211":1159,"2212":1770,"2213":1100,"2214":1469,"2215":144,"2216":146,"2217":139,"2218":132,"2219":140,"2220":131,"2221":138,"2222":133,"2223":136,"2224":135,"2225":145,"2226":11,"2227":12,"2228":114,"2229":117,"2230":116,"2231":115,"2232":112,"2233":113,"2234":1241,"2235":1194,"2236":1769,"2237":1403,"2238":53,"2239":56,"2240":55,"2241":54,"2242":451,"2243":467,"2244":64,"2245":66,"2246":65,"2247":33,"2248":1161,"2249":1262,"2250":1195,"2251":280,"2252":230,"2253":111,"2254":110,"2255":1136,"2256":291,"2257":119,"2258":118,"2259":120,"2260":1153,"2261":34,"2262":1264,"2263":1196,"2264":1399,"2265":1373,"2266":1317,"2267":88,"2268":89,"2269":1466,"2270":805,"2271":36,"2272":1309,"2273":1197,"2274":2053,"2275":1106,"2276":296,"2277":822,"2278":1334,"2279":1298,"2280":1242,"2281":2047,"2282":1299,"2283":482,"2284":1233,"2285":1472,"2286":827,"2287":1255,"2288":26,"2289":27,"2290":1387,"2291":1386,"2292":469,"2293":158,"2294":159,"2295":155,"2296":156,"2297":157,"2298":160,"2299":154,"2300":161,"2301":830,"2302":101,"2303":106,"2304":102,"2305":103,"2306":104,"2307":105,"2308":1771,"2309":1440,"2310":1761,"2311":29,"2312":2050,"2313":1198,"2314":2321,"2315":1376,"2316":1414,"2317":1391,"2318":1424,"2319":295,"2320":1455,"2321":1457,"2322":1406,"2323":1265,"2324":1123,"2325":1415,"2326":1363,"2327":1425,"2328":1762,"2329":24,"2330":28,"2331":1137,"2332":312},"orderedDocs":[[1990,"**Bare** changes the metadata content of every ledger except the protocol-upgrade one. There are no classic events, no fee events, and v0 meta extensions."],[1938,"**Fixed seeds.** Every keypair is `sha256('xdrproof:' + name)`; the root account comes from the passphrase."],[1939,"**Fixed time.** Ledger n closes at `1767225600 + n × 30 days`."],[1991,"**Galexie's** extra flags change no classic ledger, and 46 Soroban ones: every ledger with a contract call. In those, each contract event appears twice, in the operation's events and again among the diagnostic events."],[1941,"**Ledger 2 is always the protocol upgrade,** and never an entry."],[1940,"**No RPC, no simulation.** Transactions go straight to core's `tx` endpoint, and ledgers close with `manualclose`."],[2119,"**XDRProof turns each of those shapes into a test everyone can run.** One team's incident becomes every team's regression test, and one SDK's fix becomes a check on all of them."],[1998,"`@stellar/stellar-xdr-json` 30.0.0, rs-stellar-xdr compiled to WASM, refuses 13 corpus variants that stellar-core wrote (`depth limit exceeded`): 8 whose authorization tree is 245 levels deep, the deepest that applies, and 5 at 246, which core includes and traps. The package hard-codes `XDR_MAX_DEPTH = 500`, set to mirror the Soroban host's budget limit, and applies it to the whole `LedgerCloseMeta`, whose path down to the auth tree is deeper. js-stellar-sdk 17.4.0, go-stellar-sdk v0.9.0, both Python decoders and native rs-stellar-xdr read them. This is finding F-1 on Upstream bugs; it is not filed upstream yet."],[2029,"`caps/registry.json` is the blueprint for the corpus. Each **hazard** is a named way a reader of the Stellar ledger breaks. Some examples:"],[1995,"`fee_charged` is then the full declared maximum, with no refund change and no refund event. A reader that computes the fee as the charge minus the refund, or that expects a refund for every Soroban transaction, gets it wrong."],[2177,"`js@17.4.0` and `python-xdr@0.2.1` read every corpus variant exactly as rs-stellar-xdr does: the bytes, the SEP-0051 JSON and every expected fact."],[2226,"`make all` runs verify, oracle, coverage, generate, conformance and replay."],[2227,"`make build` is not a check: it compiles `catalog/` into `entries/` from the runs of `make generate` and `mined/`, in minutes. See Catalog."],[1559,"`make conformance` runs a vector with the same kind of collision (a two-entry map whose keys both read as \"1\") through js-stellar-sdk builds before and after the fix. The recorded matrix shows 17.2.0 and 17.2.1 keeping 1 of 2 entries, and 17.3.0 rejecting the map."],[2191,"`make coverage` counts every arm in an entry's file, including arms from other transactions that happen to share its ledger. `make coverage-report` is stricter. An entry **reaches** an arm only when its own transaction (envelope, fee changes, apply meta) or its ledger's own shape (header, transaction-set phases, upgrades, evicted keys) contains it. Every arm no entry reaches is classified in `coverage/exclusions.json`, with the stellar-core source line that decides it. The run fails if an arm is in neither list, or in both."],[1992,"`make generate` re-measures this into `recipes/<lane>/profiles/`."],[2202,"`make generate` runs **10 pairs**, which is 20 fresh standalone cores, 6 at a time. There is no RPC, no network, and no keys or funds."],[1954,"`make generate` runs 10 configurations twice each: classic P30 on both passphrases, Soroban P30 and P28 on both passphrases, and the galexie and bare profiles at P30 mainnet for each lane. It checks that every shipped generated variant is reproduced. See Generate."],[1624,"`make replay` feeds testnet ledgers 4437356–4437359 to three real wallet-backend builds through a mock stellar-rpc:"],[1505,"`make replay` feeds this entry's **P28** variant to two wallet-backend builds through a mock stellar-rpc. Build `764a4f5b` **drops the trustline**: no TRUSTLINE/ADD state change is recorded. Build `c152783c`, \"record SAC-created trustline state changes\" (#734, the fix for #731), records it. See Replay."],[1930,"`make verify` also runs `tools/mined-verify.mjs`. Every file must match its hash, round-trip byte for byte through native rs-stellar-xdr, and carry the recorded sequence and protocol. Every finding's transaction and JSON path must be present. `make coverage` reports the union arms these ledgers reach: ** of **."],[16,"`make verify` and `make oracle` check the built entries like any other. `make novelty` then fails if the new entry adds nothing another entry doesn't already hold."],[1909,"`make verify` checks the schema, sizes and hashes, a byte-for-byte round trip through native rs-stellar-xdr, the focus transaction and every fact. `make oracle` checks that each fact's values also appear in what stellar-core's own decoder and the schema walker read."],[1916,"`manifest.json` is generated from the entries, one row per variant. `make verify` fails if it is out of date."],[2329,"`manifest.json` is rebuilt from the entries. Without `--write`, verify fails if the committed file has drifted."],[1927,"`mined/` holds those as real `LedgerCloseMeta`, fetched from SDF's public data lake and located with BigQuery over the public Hubble dataset. The queries are in `mined/queries/`."],[2288,"`replay/lib/derive.mjs` reads the ledger with rs-stellar-xdr and lists the **probes**: the facts a correct indexer has stored after ingesting it. They come from the ledger alone."],[2289,"`replay/lib/mock-rpc.mjs` serves the ledger as stellar-rpc v30.0.1 would: `getLedgers`, `getHealth`, `getLatestLedger`, `getNetwork`, `getVersionInfo`, and `getLedgerEntries` from the state the ledger leaves behind. Pagination, page limits and validation errors follow stellar-rpc word for word."],[2330,"`tools/mined-verify.mjs` checks every mined ledger. It must match its hash and size, round-trip through the native reader, and carry the recorded sequence and protocol. Every finding's transaction and JSON path must be present."],[2311,"<Callout title=\"A new failure, a changed one and a fixed one all fail the run\">`replay/expectations/<adapter>@<target>.json` lists every variant that is not `handled`, with the exact probes that failed, the cause and the upstream issue. It also pins the set of variants judged (their count and a sha256 of their ids), so none can drop out of a run unnoticed.</Callout>"],[27,"<Callout title=\"Authoring aid\">`node tools/inspect.mjs <lane> <step> [variant]` reads a `make generate` run and prints the focus transaction's result and fee, and for each operation the kinds of its changes and its events.</Callout>"],[1931,"<Callout title=\"Network data, not entries\">These ledgers were written by SDF's Galexie with its default flags, so their metadata differs from a default node's (see Found while building). Most are not corpus entries: entries carry facts and hazards, and these carry findings. The catalog also compiles entries from them: entries so far, built from of these ledgers, the signed-payload signer among them.</Callout>"],[1558,"<Callout title=\"Not run yet\">The schema says SDK checks belong to the conformance runner, but no tool runs them yet. Today the runner uses its own vectors, below.</Callout>"],[2247,"<Callout title=\"Placement is a claim, not a measurement\">A placement is text the author wrote. So `make novelty` lists every entry told apart only by placement, and flags the ones wholly contained in one other entry: for each such pair, the facts must check a different thing.</Callout>"],[2261,"<Callout title=\"What it does not check\">It checks that a value is present in a reader's output, not that it sits at the fact's path; the path is checked by Verify.</Callout>"],[1988,"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"For indexers\">Never depend on the order of changes within an operation.</Callout>"],[2271,"<Callout type=\"warn\" title=\"For indexers\">Never depend on the order of changes within an operation.</Callout>"],[1910,"<File name=\"<id>.json\" />"],[1911,"<File name=\"entry.json\" />"],[1915,"<File name=\"entry.schema.json\" />"],[1914,"<File name=\"manifest.json\" />"],[1913,"<File name=\"p28-testnet-generated.xdr\" />"],[1912,"<File name=\"p30-mainnet-generated.xdr\" />"],[23,"| `at`                                     | Resolves to                